cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Yeliztli in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Yeliztli: a privacy-first personal-genomics analysis platform"
abstract: >-
  Yeliztli is a local-only platform that annotates consumer genotyping-array raw
  data (23andMe, AncestryDNA) against public clinical and population databases
  and organises the results into focused analysis modules (pharmacogenomics,
  ancestry, carrier status, hereditary-risk panels, wellness traits). It runs
  entirely on the user's machine; genotypes are never uploaded. For research and
  educational use only — not a clinical-grade test.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Campos-Chavez
    given-names: Eduardo
    alias: bioedca
repository-code: "https://github.com/bioedca/Yeliztli"
url: "https://bioedca.github.io/Yeliztli/"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
keywords:
